  "prefLabel": "Env-A 105.50 Whole tree chip",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 105.50 “Whole tree chip” means a piece of wood produced by chipping a whole tree, including wood, bark, tree tops, limbs, and logging residue.\n\nSource. #6342-A, eff 9-28-96; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.303), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.215), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); renumbered by #10549, (from Env-A 101.217); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.218) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
